{
  "name": "whiskers",
  "personality": "Aloof but curious. Not hostile, but not friendly either—he treats the mansion like his territory, and everyone else is just a guest who hasn't been properly vetted yet. He watches. Always watches. From high places, from shadows, from the corner of your eye.",
  "description": "",
  "base_description": "A lean, gray tabby with a coat like weathered slate, darker striping along his flanks and a pale underbelly. His eyes are a sharp, pale amber—almost gold, and they catch the light in a way that feels too aware. His tail is thick and plush, like a fox's brush, and he carries it high and slow, like a banner that says I own this place. His fur is always clean, always groomed, even in the dust and decay of the mansion.",
